1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,035
How does this laptop setup become a production system?

2
00:00:03,035 --> 00:00:05,654
First, we build a container image for the app.

3
00:00:05,654 --> 00:00:11,083
A Helm chart deploys it to Kubernetes, with three replicas behind one service.

4
00:00:11,083 --> 00:00:17,940
Actuator's liveness and readiness probes tell Kubernetes when to restart a pod, and when to send it traffic.

5
00:00:17,940 --> 00:00:21,488
Secrets come from Vault at startup, and never from files.

6
00:00:21,488 --> 00:00:28,273
With three replicas, every scheduled job would run three times, so ShedLock lets only one of them run.

7
00:00:28,273 --> 00:00:33,428
Kill a pod in the middle of a payment, and the payment still resolves exactly once.

8
00:00:33,428 --> 00:00:36,964
Next, moving one module out into its own service.

